Package: print-archive
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: EduhCommerce <eduhcommerce@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/ehstbr/PyCUPS
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3-gi, python3-cups, python3-pypdf, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0, gir1.2-soup-3.0, poppler-utils, cups-client, cups-daemon, pkexec, libglib2.0-bin
Description: PyCUPS CUPS Archive for retained print jobs
 PyCUPS browses the local CUPS job history, retrieves and previews
 retained documents, exports originals, and reprints complete jobs or selected
 PDF pages.
 .
 Its settings screen can configure retention and bounded global CUPS switches
 only after an explicit Apply action through a PolicyKit helper.
 A first-run guide can compare live values with an editable 30/90-day proposal.
 PyCUPS blocks its interface until CUPS answers fresh readiness probes after
 global settings are changed.
 Package installation and application startup never alter those values.
